(text "X-07 SIDE (directly on the expansion bus)" (at 20.00 25.00 0) (effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 2afdaf03-039d-4db0-9ffd-c79a1d42db13))
(text "J1 mates with the X-07 rear 40-pin connector; J2 is the pass-through\nslot for I/O packs, wired 1:1.  Connector parts/footprints TBD (pitch unknown).\nAD0-AD7 carry A0-A7 while ALE is high (NSC800 multiplexed bus).\nOriginal X-720: GND via 1R (R351/R352), VCC2 via 120R (R250); not yet\nreproduced.  VEX/VCC2/KACL/INTR/BUZZ go to the Power and Video sheets." (at 20.00 150.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 80382f74-1482-46a4-908d-1eb67846aaeb))
(text "MEMORY MAP (IO/~{M} = 0, U5)\n8000-87FF ~{MEM_8000}  VRAM block 0\n8800-8FFF ~{MEM_8800}  VRAM block 1\n9000-97FF ~{MEM_9000}  VRAM block 2\n9800-9FFF ~{MEM_9800}  I/O pack ROM (slot, not buffered)\nA000-AFFF ~{ROM_CS}    TV BASIC ROM\n\nI/O MAP (IO/~{M} = 1, U6)\n80-87 ~{IO_80}  CG ROM access (Video sheet)\n88-8F ~{IO_88}  CG ROM access (Video sheet)\n90-97 W: mode register U11, R: status U12\n98-9F W: ~{SLOT_WR} (I/O pack low address latch, TBD)\n\nU4 only drives the X-07 bus for 8000-97FF, A000-AFFF\nand ports 80-97.  Unused gate inputs are tied to GND." (at 20.00 205.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 6f1b3105-5f7c-4cca-9818-de9daddd8e9d))
(text "PORT 90 BITS (book fig. 9)\nW: D7 FSR  D6 A/~{G}  D5 +1K  D4-D2 GM2-GM0  D1-D0 CSS1/CSS0\nR: D7 FS   D6 INT   D5-D0 = 0\nD1/D0 cut off in the scan; assumed CSS." (at 280.00 135.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid ace9de26-7c3b-4e3f-907f-cec143f0b778))
)
